      "content": "Relying solely on a limitations section to paper over a flawed statistical method is generally insufficient for a centerpiece piece aiming for high impact. While you might gain speed, this approach risks serious retractions if the statistical error is scrutinized later. I strongly advise addressing the variance issue directly by re-calculating the statistics using a standard, appropriate estimator first. This proactive correction mitigates the risk while still allowing you to meet your deadline with a significantly stronger paper.",
